  "body": "Closes #1063\nClaim: cloud/i970-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i970-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/r1093-opus round 1 on `3fbb8a0`, REQUEST CHANGES; cloud/r1063-opus-review round 2 on `6e668fe`, APPROVE)\n\n#1062 / #1064 are merged, so this branches from `dev-swift`.\n\n## Problem\nThe picker « Style des messages » only says « Moderne » or « Classique »: nothing shows what the choice changes (operator feedback of 2026-11-17).\n\n## Cause\nNo preview. The difference lives in `reader.css` (`.style-modern` / `.style-classic`), selected by `TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:90`.\n\n## Change\n- `StylePreviewContent` (pure, testable): a `ReaderPage` of two sample messages (an odd and an even one, pseudos « Exemple A » / « Exemple B », no image, no link), the document built by the **real** `TopicHTMLBuilder.document` with the chosen style, and one sentence per style, written from the verified CSS: header tint 3 % against 15 % (`reader.css:117-118`, `:215`) and the text under the pseudo (`--indent`, `:127`, `:132`) against the left margin. The even-message band (`reader.css:88`) is the same in both styles, so the sentences do not claim it (round 1: the first wording said it alternates per style and « sous l’avatar »; both were wrong).\n  - Moderne : « texte aligné sous le pseudo, en-têtes à peine teintés. »\n  - Classique : « en-têtes teintés, texte à la marge. »\n- `StylePreview` view: the reader's `ReaderWebView` + `ReaderWebController` (theme, density and text size from the environment as in the reader), created when the settings screen shows it, one document per style change (token), scrolling off, `allowsHitTesting(false)`, hidden from VoiceOver; its height follows Dynamic Type (`@ScaledMetric`) and the in-app text size (`textScale`), so the second message is not cut. Third-party images off; the fetcher is never asked (no image in the sample).\n- `SettingsView`: one line under the picker.\n\nWhy not wider: nothing changes in the reader, `reader.css` or `TopicHTMLBuilder`.\n\n## Tests (`StylePreviewTests`, app-hosted Swift Testing; written without Xcode, built by the compile check (green on the head), run by CI when ready)\n- the document carries `<body class=\"nosig style-…\">` for the chosen style and not the other's class (both styles);\n- two articles, both sample pseudos and texts, no real member;\n- no `http:` / `https:`, no `` ˋ&lt;imgˋ, no ˋ&lt;a ˋ in either style; ``\n- the sentence per style, word for word, and a test that no sentence claims the alternation or the avatar indent as a style difference (fails on the round-1 wording).\nThey fail without the change (`StylePreviewContent` does not exist before it).\n\n## Device check (to list on #893)\nSwitching the style changes the preview at once, in light and dark; **at 70 % and 130 % text size and at accessibility Dynamic Type sizes both messages stay fully visible** (the page keeps some fixed pixels, `reader.css:120`, `:124`: if the second message is cut, add a small fixed slack to the frame); the preview does not scroll and VoiceOver skips it, reading the sentence.\n\n## Ledger\nNo legacy behaviour changes: the legacy picker (`AppSettingsView.swift:471-472` @ 87fe0d1c) has no preview; this is a SwiftHFR addition (no ledger entry).\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFtuGduNx3JqYjNFU4",
