   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1093-opus, head 3fbb8a0): REQUEST CHANGES**\n\n1. **Medium**, `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/StylePreview.swift:36-37` (and the doc comment at :8-9): the sentence does not match the CSS. The issue asked to \"adjust the wording to the verified table\", but the wording was copied unchanged.\n   - **Even-message band.** `reader.css:88` (`article.message:nth-of-type(even) { background: var(--surface-alt) }`) has no style condition, so even messages are tinted in **both** styles. The comment \"the band of every even message (classic only)\" is false.\n   - **\"en-têtes … alternés\" (classic).** `:223-226` paints the even classic header as the 15 % tint over `--background`, and an odd article also sits on `--background`. So classic headers are the **same** on odd and even messages. The thing that alternates is the message body, in both styles.\n   - **\"texte aligné sous l'avatar\" (modern).** `--indent` is 2.7rem, which is the avatar (2.2em) plus the gap (0.5em) (`:27-30`: \"it starts under the pseudo\"). So the text sits under the **pseudo**, not under the avatar.\n   - Failing case: a VoiceOver user is told something the reader does not do, because the web view is hidden and this sentence is all they get.\n   - Fix: for example « Moderne : texte aligné sous le pseudo, en-têtes à peine teintés. Classique : en-têtes teintés, texte à la marge. » Correct the doc comment and the test to match.\n2. **Low**, `StylePreview.swift:51` / `:62`: `@ScaledMetric` follows Dynamic Type but ignores the in-app text size, which ranges from 70 to 130 %. The web view applies that size through `--text-scale`.\n   - Failing case: at 130 % on a 320 pt-wide phone, the two messages need roughly 250 pt (estimated from the CSS; I have not measured it). Scrolling is off, so the second message, the one that shows the alternation, is cut.\n   - Fix: `@Environment(\\.textScale)` and `.frame(height: scale.scaled(height))`.\n3. **Detail**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Settings/StylePreviewTests.swift:33-36`: the sentence test copies the strings, so it can only fail on a wording change, never on a wrong claim. It passed finding 1. The other three tests are sound: removing the style, adding an `avatarURL` or adding a message makes them fail.\n\n**Verified**\n- Head `3fbb8a08` checked out in a throwaway worktree.\n- SwiftLint on the 3 files: clean.\n- Read `reader.css` lines 15-95 and 115-250, `TopicHTMLBuilder` lines 50-140, and `ReaderWebController`, `+Presence`, `ReaderWebView`, and the theme and text-scale environment injection.\n  - Lifecycle: no retain cycle (the proxies and the pan watcher hold the controller weakly, and no events are set). `windowDidChange` never stops the web view (`disappeared` stays false).\n  - No request can leave: the CSP allows only the `hfrreader:` scheme, there is no `<img>` or `<a>`, and `autoLoadsThirdPartyImages` returns false.\n  - No interaction: hit-testing and scrolling are off.\n  - The two articles are adjacent siblings under `<main>`, so `nth-of-type` counts them as odd and even.\n- No Xcode here: the tests were not run. CI's \"App build + tests\" was skipped because the PR is a draft (#477). Only the compile check is green.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
