   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1063-opus-review, round 2, head 6e668fe): APPROVE**\n\nFindings:\n\n1. Detail. `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/StylePreview.swift:64`: the frame now scales linearly (`@ScaledMetric(.body)` × in-app factor). The page keeps a few fixed px that do not scale: `padding-bottom: 10px` on the content (reader.css:124) and the classic `padding-top: 8px` (:120). At 70 %, the frame shrinks by about 66 pt and the text by about 55 pt, so a tight layout at 100 % could lose about 10 pt at the bottom. Line wrapping at accessibility sizes also does not grow linearly. This cannot be measured on Linux. Fix: none needed if the hand check on #893 at 70 % and AX sizes shows both messages. Otherwise add a small fixed slack (`textScale.scaled(height) + 20`).\n\nChecked and true against reader.css:\n- (a) Modern \"à peine teintés\": 3 % at :117. Classic \"teintés\": 15 % at :118, :215 and :223-226.\n- (a) \"sous le pseudo\": `--indent` = scale × 2.7rem (:32, :127, :132). The header's font is scale × 1rem (:74), and its avatar plus gap is 2.2em + 0.5em = 2.7em, so the text lines up with the pseudo, as the comment at :28-30 says.\n- (a) Classic \"à la marge\": no padding-left on the content, so the text starts at the article's 1em edge (:131).\n- (a) The 8 px classic padding-top (:120) is not mentioned and is not contradicted.\n- (a) The even band is the same in both styles (:88). \"pour voir l'alternance\" is accurate and does not present the band as a style difference.\n- (b) `textScale` is injected at the app root (`SwiftHFRApp.swift:80` → `appTypography`, `ListDensity.swift:183`), above the Settings screen. `ReaderWebView.swift:16` reads the same value for `--text-scale`, so the frame and the page follow one factor.\n- (c) The new test fails on the round-1 sentences: \"avatar\" in the modern one, \"alternés\" in the classic one. The `Set` count guards against two identical sentences. `ThemeStyle` is `CaseIterable` (HFRModels).\n- (d) No problem in the diff. The compile check on this head is green, but the app tests have not run.\n\n**Verified**: the 3fbb8a08..6e668fe2 diff in a throwaway worktree, read against reader.css, TextScale.swift, ListDensity.swift, SwiftHFRApp.swift, ReaderWebView.swift and SettingsView.swift. `swiftlint lint --strict` on both changed files: rc=0. The app and its tests cannot be built on Linux and were not run.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
